We’ll work from your Mini Parking System assessment. I won’t write any code for you. I’ll break down the logic and algorithm step by step so you can implement the methods yourself and write tests to verify them.

Your assessment requires a parking lot with 20 slots, where `0` means empty and `1` means occupied. Cars can enter the first available slot from left to right or a specified empty slot. Cars can leave by specifying their slot number, and the parking status must be displayed after each action.&#x20;

